t_uuid":"89a14ec8-d4d9-4cd7-8450-955417af8904","position":{"commit_sha":"82a6eb339405631d4c56c10b467b0e25d8dda2e6","position":"1787099098790998001-89a14ec8-d4d9-4cd7-8450-955417af8904"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cff6787441b642fb709220f47aaf70cbca0b880a2691cefa523f9a869a97af6a","event_uuid":"1cf66df9-3099-4159-9f83-ebee038c750b","position":{"commit_sha":"c7a5b906bb20856122a3ded5fb404b207eb726bd","position":"1787099105117510001-1cf66df9-3099-4159-9f83-ebee038c750b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-232_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"03a4b6e2-5666-42d5-8aaa-0906798afc8f","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC evidence map (all 8 satisfied; 27/27 tests green in tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py). Landed as Gerrit change 1880 (commit ffb1fee5ac) with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. AC1 legacy/unknown-field byte round trip + no eager write -> test_unknown_fields_round_trip_byte_identical, test_save_writes_exact_sorted_indented_newline_bytes, test_construction_over_seeded_state_performs_no_eager_write, test_construction_over_absent_state_creates_no_files. AC2 unconditional save attempts rotation before live -> test_save_without_in_memory_change_still_persists_rotation plus test_save_persists_rotation_before_replacing_live (a destination-discriminated os.replace order spy; note binding_repository.os and get_rotation.os are the SAME stdlib module, so module-level patching cannot discriminate). AC3 live fails closed / retired fails open with best-effort alerting -> test_corrupt_live_state_raises_value_error_and_preserves_the_file, test_corrupt_live_error_names_the_file_and_recovery_route, test_corrupt_retired_state_fails_open_alerts_and_preserves_the_file. AC4 rotation failure leaves sidecar old, live new, inline floor retained, no raise -> test_rotation_tempfile_failure_keeps_sidecar_old_and_live_new_with_floor, test_rotation_replace_failure_keeps_sidecar_old_and_live_new_with_floor. AC5 two-save fault/recovery convergence -> test_next_save_after_rotation_failure_converges_sidecar_from_inline_floor. AC6 retired write failure leaves retired+live old and raises -> test_retired_tempfile_failure_keeps_retired_and_live_old_and_raises, test_retired_replace_failure_keeps_retired_and_live_old_and_raises. AC7 live failure leaves live old, retains earlier sidecar/retired write, cleans temp, raises -> test_live_replace_failure_after_rotation_keeps_live_old_and_raises, test_live_tempfile_failure_keeps_live_old_and_raises, test_live_failure_after_successful_retired_write_retains_the_tombstone (this last one constructs the exact retired-first/live-failed overlap RP-02 S3 later repairs). AC8 alert failure swallowed without altering the state write -> test_alert_persistence_failure_is_swallowed_and_preserves_the_state_write. HELD-OUT TDD: all 27 tests RED first against a signature-only scaffold; the implementation subagent saw ONLY the 12 happy-path tests (the 15 fault/corruption tests were physically moved out of the worktree) and reported 1 attempt to green. Validation found 2 failures, both diagnosed as MY test defects and fixed - the os-module patch collision above, and a dedup test over-specified against an aspirational docstring (a differential probe proved BindingStore emits 2 alerts too, because alert records never stamp timestamp_ns so is_deduped's 24h window can never match). 5 defect-seeded mutations each go RED; a behavior-preserving rename keeps all 27 green. binding_repository.py is 360 LOC; binding_store.py is untouched at 799 (facade cutover is T2).","timestamp":1787098546266260001}],"created_at":1787027406115418001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ee4aba2d-1aa0-4645-9153-7a3a6ca4cb3f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8ddb-79b4-a066-4197"}],"description":"## Context\nBinding persistence shares `binding_store.py` with lifecycle policy. Extraction is unsafe until byte layout, load rules, unconditional save behavior, and ordered partial-state failures have direct oracles.\n\n## Outcome\nCreate `BindingRepository` as the sole owner of live, retired, rotation, and alert files. It retains the original dictionaries, exact serialization, load behavior, and current unconditional save boundary. No facade cutover or new dirty gate occurs in this task.\n\n## Plan\n1. Start with direct failing tests over legacy/unknown-field fixtures, construction with no eager write, unconditional save, and exact sorted/indented/trailing-newline bytes.\n2. Implement path ownership, open typed views over original dictionaries, tempfile cleanup, and per-file `os.replace`. Current-code oracles are `BindingStore._load`, `_load_retired`, `_save_retired`, `_alert`, `save`, `_retire`, and `get_rotation.save` on the reviewed base.\n3. Pin the existing corruption contract: corrupt live JSON raises `ValueError` and preserves the file; corrupt retired JSON returns empty, preserves the file, and attempts a deduped alert; alert failure is swallowed.\n4. Pin exact persistence cuts:\n   - rotation tempfile/write/replace failure: rotation stays old; live is replaced with new bytes retaining inline `last_get_pass`; failure is swallowed.\n   - next-save recovery after that cut: remove the injected failure, call save again, and assert the rotation sidecar converges from retained inline `last_get_pass` before live replacement.\n   - live tempfile/write/replace failure after successful rotation: rotation is new; live stays old; temp is cleaned; failure raises.\n   - retired tempfile/write/replace failure: retired and live stay old; temp is cleaned; failure raises.\n   - live replacement failure during retirement: retired is new; live stays old; temp is cleaned; failure raises.\n   - alert persistence failure after a successful state write changes no state-file result and is swallowed.\n5. Keep the current retired-first and rotation-before-live order. Make no multi-file atomicity, journal, eager-load rewrite, deep-copy, publication, or write-elision claim.\n\n## Testing\nUse real temporary files and injected cuts at each named operation. Assert exact surviving bytes, cleanup, and exception outcome. Add a two-save rotation test: fail the first sidecar write, verify the inline floor survives in live, allow the second sidecar write, then verify sidecar/live convergence. The current reviewed functions above are the characterization source; captured fixtures make the oracle durable.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Legacy and unknown-field fixtures round-trip to byte-identical sorted/indented/newline JSON, and construction performs no eager write.\n- [x] Calling save without an in-memory change still attempts rotation persistence before live replacement.\n- [x] Corrupt live state fails closed; corrupt retired state fails open with best-effort alerting.\n- [x] Rotation persistence failure leaves rotation old and live new with the inline floor, without raising.\n- [x] After one injected rotation failure, the next successful save writes the retained inline floor to the sidecar before live replacement; verified by the two-save fault/recovery test.\n- [x] Retired persistence failure leaves retired/live old and raises.\n- [x] Live persistence failure leaves live old, retains any earlier successful sidecar/retired write, cleans its temp, and raises.\n- [x] Alert persistence failure is swallowed and does not alter the successful state-file result.\n\n## Out of scope\nFacade delegation, lifecycle extraction, tickets publication, recovery cutover, and dirty/write-elision optimization remain outside this task.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_repository.py","reason":"New byte-preserving persistence and unit-of-work owner."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py","reason":"Direct byte, corruption, dirty-gate, and fault-cut oracles."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","5142-4dbf-9469-4672"],["relates_to","8ddb-79b4-a066-4197"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5142-4dbf-9469-4672","parent_status_uuid":"89a14ec8-d4d9-4cd7-8450-955417af8904","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp02","binding-store","tdd"],"ticket_id":"2c81-7119-fb6b-44b1","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S1 T1 — Build the byte-preserving binding repository","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_repository.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC8","dd_text":"Byte format, unconditional save, corruption, rotation failure/retry convergence, retired/live fault cuts, cleanup, alert failure"}]},"source_event_uuids":["e21c94c2-7d33-4c54-8e9b-287943a8ded5","0b0dc575-3e80-4f96-80f1-45157c133c1d","c3bd60e7-7144-4924-ab17-1b1edacd3130","6515c9fa-da2e-40d2-a173-8b94b0f3356b","c2360ca7-59b2-4ec0-8262-2a32ea945d1a","c0fab0e9-4e44-44b7-9943-5806d17b1c17","5f08afe0-0784-431a-ab27-e32a34e4f56b","c4d2136a-3e50-4b6d-881c-7aae662094a5","ee4aba2d-1aa0-4645-9153-7a3a6ca4cb3f","8ff62604-49c3-47fd-a4c1-2487f41c5d4c","4c3fae4e-cbb5-4dc0-8d91-b0580f8e64b5","4d0a0d10-d44c-4061-8bc0-ebbbc45ddfe6","89a14ec8-d4d9-4cd7-8450-955417af8904","1cf66df9-3099-4159-9f83-ebee038c750b"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787104634055488001,"uuid":"a2f776ce-7b58-470e-8a44-ff8cc944796f"}